# π² Processing-in-Interconnect: CBS and ATS Shaper RTL

SystemVerilog RTL for the two Time-Sensitive Networking (TSN) traffic shapers used in the **π² (Processing-in-Interconnect)** paradigm, where the scheduling logic already present in Ethernet switches is repurposed to perform neural computation:

| Module | Standard | π² role |
|---|---|---|
| `pi2_cbs` | IEEE 802.1Qav Credit-Based Shaper (CBS) | **π² neuron** (ReLU-like activation via credit accumulation) |
| `pi2_ats_full` | IEEE 802.1Qcr Asynchronous Traffic Shaper (ATS) | **π² synapse** (weight applied as a timing delay on spikes/frames) |

The idea is that routing energy becomes computation: a spiking/event-driven network can run on the interconnect itself, with only small extensions to standard shaper hardware.

This RTL accompanies the paper:

> M. Srivatsav, C. Bhattacharyya, S. Chakrabartty, and C. S. Thakur, *"When Routers, Switches and Interconnects Compute: A Processing-in-Interconnect Paradigm for Scalable Neuromorphic AI,"* arXiv:2508.19548, 2025.
